# Generated by TestFlowAssistant — Stage: Scenarios (draft, not yet reviewed)

Feature: Checkout Payment — Card Payment with Promo Code and Stock Validation
  As an E-commerce Customer
  I want my final charged amount to correctly reflect promo and stock adjustments, with a single debit and no exposed card data
  So that I am charged accurately, only once, and my payment details stay protected

  Background:
    Given the customer has an item in the cart
    And the checkout page is loaded with card payment selected as the payment method

  @smoke @critical @risk-critical
  Scenario: Captured amount matches cart total after promo code recalculation
    Given the cart has a known total before a promo code is applied
    When the customer applies a valid promo code and submits payment
    Then the captured amount equals the recalculated cart total after the discount
    And the order confirmation displays the same recalculated total

  @smoke @critical @risk-critical
  Scenario: Exactly one debit is recorded when retrying payment after a timeout
    Given a payment submission has timed out without a confirmed response
    When the customer retries the payment submission using the same idempotency key
    Then exactly one authorization is recorded for the transaction
    And no duplicate debit appears against the customer's account

  @regression @risk-high
  Scenario: Order does not confirm without a successful capture callback
    Given a payment authorization has been initiated for an order
    When the capture callback from the payment gateway fails to arrive
    Then the order remains in a pending state
    And no order confirmation is sent to the customer

  @boundary @edge-case @risk-high
  Scenario: Payment capture is blocked when stock is depleted at the moment of submission
    Given an item's stock quantity reaches zero at the same moment the customer submits payment
    When the payment submission is processed
    Then the payment capture is blocked
    And the order status remains unconfirmed pending stock re-validation

  @security @risk-high
  Scenario: CVV and card number are masked across UI, API, and logs
    Given the customer has entered card payment details at checkout
    When the payment is submitted for authorization
    Then the CVV does not appear in any UI, API response, or log
    And the card number is shown only as first 6 and last 4 digits in the UI, API response, and logs

  @security @negative @risk-high
  Scenario: Promo code field rejects injection and oversized input
    Given the customer is on the checkout page with the promo code field available
    When the customer submits an oversized or script-injection string as the promo code
    Then the system rejects the input without applying any discount
    And no injected or oversized value appears in the application logs

  @negative @risk-medium
  Scenario: Malformed promo code is rejected and charged amount is unaffected
    Given the cart has a valid item and total
    When the customer enters a malformed promo code and attempts to apply it
    Then the promo code is rejected with a validation message
    And the charged amount remains equal to the original cart total

  @regression @data-driven @risk-medium
  Scenario Outline: Promo code stacking and expiry produce the correct charged amount
    Given the cart already has a promo code applied yielding a discounted total
    When the customer attempts to apply promo code "<promo_code>" of type "<promo_type>"
    Then the promo code application result is "<expected_result>"
    And the charged amount matches "<expected_amount>"

    Examples:
      | promo_type       | promo_code       | expected_result      | expected_amount                          |
      | second-stacked   | STACK2           | rejected             | previously discounted total unchanged    |
      | expired          | EXPIRED10        | rejected             | full cart total, no discount applied     |
```

